  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "413d5649-1d19-43bb-aeb2-e8e734018a23",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## **Linked List**",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "413d5649-1d19-43bb-aeb2-e8e734018a23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e7501709-821b-4a85-9427-54a4c5dbb626",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 1.Linked List Creation",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "e7501709-821b-4a85-9427-54a4c5dbb626"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e1bdff62-1b58-4c2c-a473-25b4e55c4386",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "public class Node<T> {\r\n\r\n    public T data;\r\n    public Node<T> next;\r\n\r\n    public Node(T data){\r\n        this.data = data;\r\n        this.next = null;\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// It contain data variable which will store the data of current node\r\n// Other is next variable which is another node object that will store next node for us\r\n// Then is the constructor which takes data from the user and set next node to null",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "e1bdff62-1b58-4c2c-a473-25b4e55c4386",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 7,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "0d6224fb-c943-43d9-9579-d6e1303526ed",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 2. To Take Input From The User And Print The Taken Value",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "0d6224fb-c943-43d9-9579-d6e1303526ed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d2eda5c1-da97-48a5-9bca-54c12aa368b3",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// To take input from the user\r\npublic Node<Integer> takeInput(){\r\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\r\n        int data = sc.nextInt();\r\n\r\n        if(data == -1){\r\n            return null;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> head = null;\r\n        Node<Integer> tail = null;\r\n\r\n        while(data != -1){\r\n\r\n            Node<Integer> currentNode = new Node<>(data);\r\n            if(head == null){\r\n                head = currentNode;\r\n                tail = currentNode;\r\n            }else{\r\n                tail.next = currentNode;\r\n                tail = currentNode;\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            data = sc.nextInt();\r\n        }\r\n        return head;\r\n    }\r\n   \r\n    // To print the nodes\r\n    // You can use temp to preserve the head node , so u can use it later or return it and use temp to traverse the linked likst\r\n    // temp can also be named as tail(generally people use tail in linked list as convention)\r\n    public void print(Node<Integer> head){\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> temp = head;\r\n        while(temp != null){\r\n\r\n            System.out.print(temp.data + \" \");;\r\n            temp = temp.next;\r\n        }\r\n        System.out.println();\r\n\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // To use takeInput() and print() method\r\n    Node<Integer> head = takeInput();\r\n    print(head);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "d2eda5c1-da97-48a5-9bca-54c12aa368b3",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 8,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "1 3 4 5 6 \r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "27cc5978-dcc8-4788-b332-658b42e88eb9",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 3. To get the size of Linked ",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "27cc5978-dcc8-4788-b332-658b42e88eb9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c27c088d-4d72-4788-9587-3fc2840175bd",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "\r\npublic int getLength(Node<Integer> head){\r\n        Node<Integer> temp = head;\r\n        int count = 0;\r\n\r\n        while(temp != null){\r\n            count++;\r\n            temp = temp.next;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        return count;\r\n    }",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "c27c088d-4d72-4788-9587-3fc2840175bd",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 9,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "24513c05-e1f9-4291-b7a8-08b1656794b1",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 4. To insert node at particular position",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "24513c05-e1f9-4291-b7a8-08b1656794b1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6442d422-cfcd-4c67-84e9-635e81aa5053",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "public Node<Integer> insertNode(Node<Integer> head, int num, int pos){\r\n        Node<Integer> newNode = new Node<>(num);\r\n\r\n        if(pos == 0){\r\n            newNode.next = head;\r\n            head = newNode;\r\n            return head;\r\n\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> prev = head;\r\n        int count = 0;\r\n        while(count < pos - 1 && prev != null){\r\n            prev = prev.next;\r\n            count++;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        if(prev != null){\r\n            newNode.next = prev.next;\r\n            prev.next = newNode;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n\r\n        return head;\r\n    }",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "6442d422-cfcd-4c67-84e9-635e81aa5053",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 10,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 10,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "1b854df9-11f7-4029-b432-f0ec7edc1d12",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 5. To delete a node at particular pos",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "1b854df9-11f7-4029-b432-f0ec7edc1d12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9ec75548-3662-49c0-8cbe-aafe9846c463",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "public Node<Integer> deleteNode(Node<Integer> head, int pos){\r\n\r\n        if(head == null){\r\n            return null;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        if(pos == 0){\r\n            return head.next;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> prev = head;\r\n        int count = 0;\r\n\r\n        while(count < pos - 1 && prev != null){\r\n            prev = prev.next;\r\n            count++;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        if(prev == null || prev.next == null){\r\n            return head;\r\n        }\r\n        prev.next = prev.next.next;\r\n\r\n        return head;\r\n\r\n    }",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "9ec75548-3662-49c0-8cbe-aafe9846c463",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 11,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "81dea9c5-6c9c-4e7d-a7fd-8f614ce4056a",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 6. To find a particular node",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "81dea9c5-6c9c-4e7d-a7fd-8f614ce4056a"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a566c1db-18df-4506-9b33-965d2afcf4fd",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": " public int findNode(Node<Integer> head, int num){\r\n\r\n        int pos = 0;\r\n        while(head != null){\r\n\r\n            if(head.data == num){\r\n                return pos;\r\n            }\r\n            head = head.next;\r\n            pos++;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        return -1;\r\n\r\n    }",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "a566c1db-18df-4506-9b33-965d2afcf4fd",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 12,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ee08a033-9f47-4c4c-b964-ce56d8ab5ddb",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 7. To insert in sorted linked list",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "ee08a033-9f47-4c4c-b964-ce56d8ab5ddb"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "37172cd4-87c0-46ce-b8ec-0c7bc515a886",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "public Node<Integer> insertInSorted(Node<Integer> head, int data) {\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> newNode = new Node<>(data);\r\n\r\n        // Empty list or insertion before head\r\n        if (head == null || data < head.data) {\r\n            newNode.next = head;\r\n            return newNode;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> temp = head;\r\n\r\n        // Find correct position\r\n        while (temp.next != null && temp.next.data < data) {\r\n            temp = temp.next;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        newNode.next = temp.next;\r\n        temp.next = newNode;\r\n\r\n        return head;\r\n    }",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "37172cd4-87c0-46ce-b8ec-0c7bc515a886",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 14,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "2310e519-4ac7-4991-bb75-4dbac13db0cf",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 8. To delete in sorted linked list",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "2310e519-4ac7-4991-bb75-4dbac13db0cf"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "10bd0c88-876a-456c-97e0-2e65f1f0070b",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "static Node<Integer> deleteInSorted(Node<Integer> head, int data) {\r\n\r\n        // Empty list\r\n        if (head == null) {\r\n            return null;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        // Delete head\r\n        if (head.data == data) {\r\n            return head.next;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> temp = head;\r\n\r\n        // Find node before the node to delete\r\n        while (temp.next != null && temp.next.data != data) {\r\n            temp = temp.next;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        // Delete if found\r\n        if (temp.next != null) {\r\n            temp.next = temp.next.next;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        return head;\r\n    }",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "10bd0c88-876a-456c-97e0-2e65f1f0070b",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 16,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "9a695977-a4f2-4846-80af-881663387117",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 9. To Reverse the linked list best approach",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "9a695977-a4f2-4846-80af-881663387117"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "16c2ef31-fd30-49a3-8c43-db9df828217c",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "public Node<Integer> reverseBest(Node<Integer> head){\r\n        if(head == null || head.next == null){\r\n            return head;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> ans = reverseBest(head.next);\r\n        Node<Integer> tail = head.next;\r\n        tail.next = head;\r\n        head.next = null;\r\n        return ans;\r\n        \r\n\r\n    }",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
  ]
}